        "README.md": "# Museum exhibit lookup\n\nA shared per-key query cache provides subscribe(key,options) -> unique observer\nhandle, unsubscribe(handle), online(boolean), focus(boolean), snapshot(key),\nand dispose() of observer scopes. Queries retain status (pending/success/error),\nfetchStatus (idle/fetching/paused), and data. queryFn receives a lazy signal\naccessor. Each actual access records consumption; each fetch owns its controller\nand completion. Completion is asynchronous; initial online entry is synchronous,\npaused continuation resumes on a Promise turn. First start uses network mode;\ncontinuation also needs focus. 'always' can run offline; 'offlineFirst' allows\nfirst offline entry but retry can pause. Retries use explicit scheduler handles.\nMultiple observers share one fetch. Unconsumed active work can finish into cache\nafter its view departs; consumed work is physically abortable. Cancellation\nreverts previous query data/status and settles the originating attempt. Late\nfulfillment cannot become a new attempt's data. Unknown unsubscribe is inert.\nThe component owns observer scope; the cache remains outside individual views.\nDependency versions and build/test configuration are outside the repair scope.\n\nEmbedding API: bind registers a native callable; Environment.call\nprovides newAttempt(key,number), abort(key,number), request(key,number, lazy-read\ntoken, completion token), defer(callback token), schedule(callback token,delay).\nThe request host calls queryFn with an actual AbortSignal property. Reading it\ninvokes the native consumption closure synchronously; Promise settlement later\ninvokes the native completion with {ok,value}. All observer, retry, cancellation,\nstate and cache logic executes in the target language. No native JS Promise or\nDOM claim is made. Native object identity binds query and attempt generations;\nwire handles only identify injected callbacks. \nPython cache owner and lazy context property; closure retry continuations\n",
        "VISIBLE_CHECKS.md": "Public checks are deterministic external examples, not hidden gold. They are executed after each submitted Action. Keep original task/source obligations. Checks: initial paused fetch with no remaining observer never invokes queryFn on reconnect; a remaining observer keeps the shared fetch; unconsumed active work can retain its completed cache value.\nUse the declared runtime: python3 CPython 3.8.10. The external adapter is not mounted in the model workspace; do not access scorer/reference files. Build temporary artifacts in /tmp.\n",
        "dependencies.lock.json": "{\n  \"runtime\": \"CPython 3.8.10\",\n  \"external_dependencies\": [],\n  \"stdlib_only\": true\n}\n",
        "src/workflow.py": "class Attempt:\n    def __init__(self,number,previous,options):self.number=number;self.previous=dict(previous);self.options=options;self.settled=False;self.consumed=False;self.retry_cancelled=False;self.failures=0;self.queued=False\nclass Query:\n    def __init__(self,key,data):self.key=key;self.state=dict(status='success' if data is not None else 'pending',fetchStatus='idle',data=data);self.observers=set();self.attempt=None;self.consumed=False\nclass Session:\n    def __init__(self,env,initial):self.env=env;self.cache={};self.handles={};self.online=initial.get('online',True);self.focused=initial.get('focused',True);self.serial=0;self.fetch_serial=0\n    def eligible(self,a):return self.focused and (a.options.get('networkMode','online')=='always' or self.online)\n    def active(self,q,a):return q.attempt is a and not a.settled\n    def cancel(self,q,a):\n        if a.settled:return\n        a.settled=True;q.state=dict(a.previous);q.state['fetchStatus']='idle';self.env.call('abort',q.key,a.number)\n    def invoke(self,q,a):\n        a.queued=False\n        if not self.active(q,a):return\n        q.state['fetchStatus']='fetching';q.consumed=False\n        def consume(_):q.consumed=True;return None\n        def complete(value):\n            if not self.active(q,a):return\n            if value['ok']:\n                a.settled=True;q.state.update(data=value['value'],status='success',fetchStatus='idle')\n            elif not a.retry_cancelled and a.failures<a.options.get('retry',0):\n                a.failures+=1\n                def retry(_):\n                    if not self.active(q,a):return\n                    if a.retry_cancelled:a.settled=True;q.state.update(status='error',fetchStatus='idle');return\n                    if self.eligible(a):self.invoke(q,a)\n                    else:q.state['fetchStatus']='paused'\n                self.env.call('schedule',self.env.bind(retry),a.options.get('retryDelay',10))\n            else:a.settled=True;q.state.update(status='error',fetchStatus='idle')\n        self.env.call('request',q.key,a.number,self.env.bind(consume),self.env.bind(complete))\n    def resume(self,q):\n        a=q.attempt\n        if a and self.active(q,a) and q.state['fetchStatus']=='paused' and self.eligible(a) and not a.queued:\n            a.queued=True\n            def continuation(_):\n                a.queued=False\n                if not self.active(q,a):return\n                if a.failures and a.retry_cancelled:a.settled=True;q.state.update(status='error',fetchStatus='idle');return\n                self.invoke(q,a)\n            self.env.call('defer',self.env.bind(continuation))\n    def subscribe(self,key,options):\n        q=self.cache.get(key)\n        if q is None:q=Query(key,options.get('initialData'));self.cache[key]=q\n        self.serial+=1;handle=self.serial;self.handles[handle]=q;q.observers.add(handle)\n        if q.attempt and not q.attempt.settled:q.attempt.retry_cancelled=False;self.resume(q)\n        else:\n            self.fetch_serial+=1;a=Attempt(self.fetch_serial,q.state,options);q.attempt=a;self.env.call('newAttempt',key,a.number)\n            if options.get('networkMode','online')!='online' or self.online:self.invoke(q,a)\n            else:q.state['fetchStatus']='paused'\n        return handle\n    def unsubscribe(self,handle):\n        q=self.handles.pop(handle,None)\n        if q is None:return\n        q.observers.remove(handle)\n        if not q.observers:\n            a=q.attempt\n            if a and not a.settled:\n                if q.consumed:self.cancel(q,a)\n                else:a.retry_cancelled=True\n    def handle(self,name,args):\n        if name=='subscribe':return self.subscribe(*args)\n        if name=='unsubscribe':return self.unsubscribe(*args)\n        if name=='online':self.online=args[0]\n        elif name=='focus':self.focused=args[0]\n        elif name=='snapshot':return dict(self.cache[args[0]].state)\n        elif name=='dispose':\n            for h in list(self.handles):self.unsubscribe(h)\n            return None\n        else:raise ValueError(name)\n        for q in list(self.cache.values()):self.resume(q)\n"
